### Media uploader buckets — authz boundary (uc.memory.buckets, en.memory.buckets, cr-0113)
# The unauthenticated boundary of the bucket endpoints (a `buckets` tag → its own BucketsApi), runnable against
# ANY instance — no account/scope/membership needed. Like trash.http, the AUTHENTICATED happy-path is not
# reproducible from a bare .http: listing/creating/moving needs the operator-blind scope-grant flow (a member of
# the scope) + seeded media, and the own-bucket authz (owner_key == caller) needs two members. Those — the lazy
# primary + grouping, create-sub → move → delete-reparents, foreign-owner 403, primary-not-renameable/deletable,
# and the member upload stamping user:{id} — are covered at the integration layer (MediaBucketsSliceTest) and in
# the web client's live smoke.
#
# Run: ijhttp --env-file http/media/http-client.env.json --env dev http/media/buckets.http

### 1. List a node's buckets without a bearer token → generic 401 (auth before validation)
GET {{host}}/api/scopes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/nodes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/buckets

> {%
client.test("list buckets requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}

### 2. Create a sub-bucket without a bearer token → 401
POST {{host}}/api/scopes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/nodes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/buckets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sealedName": "YnVja2V0" }

> {%
client.test("create bucket requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}

### 3. Rename a bucket without a bearer token → 401
PATCH {{host}}/api/scopes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/nodes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/buckets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sealedName": "cmVuYW1lZA==" }

> {%
client.test("rename bucket requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}

### 4. Delete a bucket without a bearer token → 401
DELETE {{host}}/api/scopes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/nodes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/buckets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

> {%
client.test("delete bucket requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
